,"Consumer Financial Protection Bureau","User charges and fees"],"sponsorBioguideId":"H001072","cosponsorCount":16,"committeeNames":[],"congressDotGovUrl":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-joint-resolution/59","industries":[{"industry":"finance-banking","confidence":0.95,"rationale":"The bill directly affects revenue from overdraft fees and regulatory compliance obligations at very large financial institutions."}],"plainSummary":"This resolution would block a Consumer Financial Protection Bureau rule that limits overdraft fees at very large banks. The rule requires these banks to either cap overdraft charges at $5, set a higher justified amount, or treat overdrafts as loans with full Truth in Lending Act disclosures. If passed, the resolution would prevent these new overdraft fee limits from taking effect.","classificationMethod":"llm","plain":{"whoItTouches":"Anyone with a bank account.","confidence":"crs-summary"},"topOverlap":{"bioguideId":"L000583","score":0.220777811455749},"overlapCount":17},"meaning":{"percentile":92.73416521876482,"median":0.010636331736930488,"n":6331,"ordinary":[],"unattributedShare":0.4611860839420577}},{"billId":"119-hr-2705","bioguideId":"N000190","cycle":2026,"score":0.027012729748894168,"matches":[{"industry":"hospitality","donorAmount":6000,"donorShare":0.07428500680945896,"billConfidence":0.4,"contribution":0.027012729748894168}],"method":{"formula":"score = Σ_industries ( donorShare(industry) × billWeight(industry) ), where billWeight = classifierConfidence / Σ classifierConfidence. Range 0–1, read as a weighted share of disclosed itemized money.","donorProfileCycle":2026,"billClassificationMethod":"llm","unclassifiedDonorShare":0.4611860839420577},"bill":{"id":"119-hr-2705","congress":119,"billType":"hr","billNumber":"2705","title":"Nuclear Family Priority Act","introducedDate":"2025-04-08","latestActionDate":"2025-04-08","latestActionText":"Referred to the House Committee on the Judiciary.","policyArea":"Immigration","subjects":[],"sponsorBioguideId":"C001132","cosponsorCount":45,"committeeNames":[],"congressDotGovUrl":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-bill/2705","industries":[{"industry":"legal","confidence":0.7,"rationale":"Immigration law firms would see changes in demand for services related to family-based visa petitions and the new nonimmigrant parent visa category."},{"industry":"hospitality","confidence":0.4,"rationale":"Reduced family immigration could affect demand for travel and lodging services related to family visits and relocation."}],"plainSummary":"This bill would sharply reduce the number of family-based immigration visas available each year, lowering the annual cap from 480,000 to 88,000. It would eliminate visa categories for siblings and married children of U.S. citizens, and would remove parents of citizens from the immediate-relative category that currently has no numerical limit. Parents of citizens would instead be eligible for a temporary visa that does not allow them to work or receive public benefits.","classificationMethod":"llm","plain":{"whoItTouches":"People applying to live here, and their families here.","confidence":"crs-summary"},"topOverlap":{"bioguideId":"K000405","score":0.033119455823821316},"overlapCount":41},"meaning":{"percentile":83.73084820723425,"median":0.010636331736930488,"n":6331,"ordinary":[],"unattributedShare":0.4611860839420577}},{"billId":"119-hr-7","bioguideId":"N000190","cycle":2026,"score":0.02427614601616306,"matches":[{"industry":"ideological-single-issue","donorAmount":3500,"donorShare":0.04333292063885106,"billConfidence":0.75,"contribution":0.012744976658485606},{"industry":"insurance","donorAmount":2500,"donorShare":0.0309520861706079,"billConfidence":0.95,"contribution":0.011531169357677453}],"method":{"formula":"score = Σ_industries ( donorShare(industry) × billWeight(industry) ), where billWeight = classifierConfidence / Σ classifierConfidence. Range 0–1, read as a weighted share of disclosed itemized money.","donorProfileCycle":2026,"billClassificationMethod":"llm","unclassifiedDonorShare":0.4611860839420577},"bill":{"id":"119-hr-7","congress":119,"billType":"hr","billNumber":"7","title":"No Taxpayer Funding for Abortion and Abortion Insurance Full Disclosure Act of 2025","introducedDate":"2025-01-22","latestActionDate":"2025-01-22","latestActionText":"Referred to the Committee on Energy and Commerce, and in addition to the Committees on the Judiciary, and Ways and Means, for a period to be subsequently determined by the Speaker, in each case for consideration of such provisions as fall within the jurisdiction of the committee concerned.","policyArea":"Health","subjects":["Abortion","Appropriations","Assault and harassment offenses","Comprehensive health care","Consumer affairs","Crimes against women","Employee benefits and pensions","Government buildings, facilities, and property","Health care costs and insurance","Health care coverage and access","Health facilities and institutions","Health programs administration and funding"],"sponsorBioguideId":"S000522","cosponsorCount":109,"committeeNames":[],"congressDotGovUrl":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-bill/7","industries":[{"industry":"insurance","confidence":0.95,"rationale":"The bill directly restricts what health insurance plans may cover and how federal subsidies interact with abortion coverage in qualified health plans."},{"industry":"health-providers","confidence":0.85,"rationale":"The bill prohibits federal health care facilities and federal employees from providing abortion services, affecting facilities that currently receive federal funds."},{"industry":"ideological-single-issue","confidence":0.75,"rationale":"Organizations focused on reproductive health policy and abortion access or restrictions have a direct stake in the regulatory framework this bill establishes."}],"plainSummary":"This bill would make permanent the restrictions on federal funding for abortion services and health insurance coverage that includes abortion. Currently, these restrictions are renewed each year through appropriations bills; the bill would apply them across all federal programs and funds. It would also prohibit qualified health plans offered through insurance marketplaces from covering abortion. The bill includes exceptions for cases of rape, incest, or when the pregnant person's life is in danger.","classificationMethod":"llm","plain":{"whoItTouches":"Anyone who buys health insurance. Anyone who pays a medical bill.","confidence":"crs-summary"},"topOverlap":{"bioguideId":"B001260","score":0.061260165720508956},"overlapCount":107},"meaning":{"percentile":80.85610488074553,"median":0.010636331736930488,"n":6331,"ordinary":[],"unattributedShare":0.4611860839420577}}],"votes":[{"id":"a64a90b759595d68f3a8d502","billId":"119-hr-7008","date":"2026-07-22T16:51:00-04:00","question":"Yea-and-Nay","result":"Passed","position":"Yea","sourceUrl":"https://clerk.house.gov/evs/2026/roll280.xml"},{"id":"2afa499bcaceefdcecfa862a","billId":"119-hr-8800","date":"2026-07-22T16:37:00-04:00","question":"Yea-and-Nay","result":"Passed","position":"Yea","sourceUrl":"https://clerk.house.gov/evs/2026/roll278.xml"},{"id":"e69a4fe10a0cc4e4d35ffc3d","billId":"119-hr-6955","date":"2026-07-21T22:05:00-04:00","question":"Yea-and-Nay","result":"Passed","position":"Yea","sourceUrl":"https://clerk.house.gov/evs/2026/roll271.xml"},{"id":"c68077c5b6dd6fe8eb42bf43","billId":"119-hres-1438","date":"2026-07-21T14:39:00-04:00","question":"Recorded Vote","result":"Passed","position":"Aye","sourceUrl":"https://clerk.house.gov/evs/2026/roll254.xml"},{"id":"3944446cfd7ceaa28fbc0515","billId":"119-hres-1438","date":"2026-07-21T14:11:00-04:00","question":"Yea-and-Nay","result":"Passed","position":"Yea","sourceUrl":"https://clerk.house.gov/evs/2026/roll253.xml"},{"id":"7d8b32832c29b7b8b63de5d9","billId":"119-hr-1118","date":"2026-07-21T14:03:00-04:00","question":"2/3 Yea-And-Nay","result":"Passed","